The data of the vt100 crate's own tests, which the crate on crates.io does
not ship. Copied from https://github.com/doy/vt100-rust at commit
eb66ffaf7d771c13303ef73b29f6f2a56fdacecf, the commit vt100 0.16.2 was
published from (its .cargo_vcs_info.json). LICENSE is that repository's
licence, which covers these files.

fixtures.tar.gz       tests/data/fixtures/, unchanged:
                      tar --sort=name --owner=0 --group=0 --numeric-owner
                      --mtime=@0 --format=ustar -cf - fixtures | gzip -9n
crawl.frames.gz       tests/data/crawl/crawl1 to crawl7625, in that order,
                      each written as its length in decimal, a newline and
                      its bytes, then gzip-compressed
weechat.typescript.gz tests/data/weechat.typescript, gzip-compressed

They are compressed because the repository checks text out with LF line
endings (.gitattributes) and these streams hold carriage returns, and
because the crawl is 7625 files.

The tests that read them are the it_*_test.go files beside testdata/.
